  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "In one hour, a crew of $4$ painters can cover $28$ square meters of a wall's surface in a newly constructed building. A construction manager has created a ratio table to determine how many square meters of the wall's surface can be covered in one hour by crews of $6$ and $9$ painters.\n\n| Painters | Square meters |\n| --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $28$ |\n| $6$ | $?$ |\n| $9$ | $?$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFrom top to bottom, what are the missing numbers in the ratio table?",
